  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Blueprint\n\nA product wipes left to right into a technical drawing with a blueprint grid, white linework, dimension lines and a red callout. A built-in red device stands in for the product; labels and colors are variables.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 2.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A hardware or product launch should show the object as an engineering drawing: measured, labelled and precise.\n- One feature of the product deserves a callout, like a sensor, a port or a button.\n- The scene should switch from a glossy product shot to a technical one in a single readable move.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The product should come apart into labelled layers instead of being measured: use exploded-view.\n- The reveal should show what is inside the device rather than its outline: use x-ray-scan.\n- The subject is a word whose outlines should draw themselves: use outline-trace.\n\nVariables:\n- blueprint_color (color): Blueprint, default \"#173C8F\"\n- line_color (color): Lines, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- callout_color (color): Callout, default \"#E5322D\"\n- product_color (color): Product, default \"#E5322D\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- width_label (string): Width label, default \"71.6 mm\"\n- height_label (string): Height label, default \"147.5 mm\"\n- callout_label (string): Callout, default \"SENSOR\"\n- title_label (string): Title block, default \"DWG A-01  SCALE 1:1\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Blueprint\n\n  A product wipes left to right into a technical drawing with a blueprint grid, white linework, dimension lines and a red callout. The built-in red device is a stand-in for the product; the labels, colors and callout text are variables.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/blueprint/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"blueprint\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"blueprint_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Blueprint\", \"description\": \"Blueprint paper color.\", \"default\": \"#173C8F\"},\n    {\"id\": \"line_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Lines\", \"description\": \"Linework and grid color.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"callout_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Callout\", \"description\": \"Callout color.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"product_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Product\", \"description\": \"Color of the built-in product before the wipe.\", \"default\": \"#E5322D\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Ground behind the product before the wipe.\", \"default\": \"#FFFFFF\"},\n    {\"id\": \"width_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Width label\", \"description\": \"Text on the horizontal dimension.\", \"default\": \"71.6 mm\"},\n    {\"id\": \"height_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Height label\", \"description\": \"Text on the vertical dimension.\", \"default\": \"147.5 mm\"},\n    {\"id\": \"callout_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Callout\", \"description\": \"Text next to the red callout.\", \"default\": \"SENSOR\"},\n    {\"id\": \"title_label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Title block\", \"description\": \"Text in the drawing title block.\", \"default\": \"DWG A-01  SCALE 1:1\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.1}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Blueprint</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #ffffff; }\n        .bp-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; overflow: hidden; }\n        .bp-stage svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; }\n        .bp-drawing { position: absolute; inset: 0; }\n        .bp-scan { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; opacity: 0; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"blueprint\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"bp-clip\" class=\"bp-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <svg id=\"bp-product\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg>\n          <div id=\"bp-drawing\" class=\"bp-drawing\"><svg id=\"bp-sheet\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></svg></div>\n          <div id=\"bp-scan\" class=\"bp-scan\"></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              if (typeof value === \"boolean\") return value;\n              if (value === \"true\") return true;\n              if (value === \"false\") return false;\n              return fallback;\n            }\n            var FPS = 30;\n            var W = root.clientWidth || 1080;\n            var H = root.clientHeight || 1920;\n\n            // Piecewise-linear map of x from inR to outR, optionally eased per segment and clamped.\n            function interp(x, inR, outR, o) {\n              o = o || {};\n              var n = inR.length;\n              var i = 0;\n              if (x >= inR[n - 1]) i = n - 2;\n              else if (x > inR[0]) { while (x > inR[i + 1]) i++; }\n              var t = (x - inR[i]) / (inR[i + 1] - inR[i]);\n              if (o.clamp !== false) t = Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t));\n              if (o.easing) t = o.easing(t);\n              return outR[i] + (outR[i + 1] - outR[i]) * t;\n            }\n            function clamp01(t) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, t)); }\n\n            // Easings with the usual names; every one maps 0..1 to 0..1.\n            var E = {\n              linear: function (t) { return t; },\n              quad: function (t) { return t * t; },\n              cubic: function (t) { return t * t * t; },\n              sin: function (t) { return 1 - Math.cos((t * Math.PI) / 2); },\n              back: function (s) { return function (t) { return t * t * ((s + 1) * t - s); }; },\n              out: function (f) { return function (t) { return 1 - f(1 - t); }; },\n              inOut: function (f) { return function (t) { return t < 0.5 ? f(t * 2) / 2 : 1 - f((1 - t) * 2) / 2; }; },\n              bezier: function (x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n                return function (x) {\n                  if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                  if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                  var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                  for (var k = 0; k < 24; k++) {\n                    var mt = 1 - t;\n                    var bx = 3 * mt * mt * t * x1 + 3 * mt * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                    if (bx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                    t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                  }\n                  var m = 1 - t;\n                  return 3 * m * m * t * y1 + 3 * m * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n                };\n              }\n            };\n\n            var SVGNS = \"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\";\n            function el(tag, attrs, parent) {\n              var e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, tag);\n              for (var k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, attrs[k]);\n              if (parent) parent.appendChild(e);\n              return e;\n            }\n\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            // Runs draw(frame) from the timeline so seeking to a time always draws the same picture.\n            function drive(frames, draw) {\n              var clock = { frame: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: frames, duration: frames / FPS, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.frame); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var blueprintColor = str(vars.blueprint_color, \"#173C8F\");\n            var lineColor = str(vars.line_color, \"#FFFFFF\");\n            var calloutColor = str(vars.callout_color, \"#E5322D\");\n            var productColor = str(vars.product_color, \"#E5322D\");\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#FFFFFF\");\n            var text = {\n              width: str(vars.width_label, \"71.6 mm\"), height: str(vars.height_label, \"147.5 mm\"),\n              callout: str(vars.callout_label, \"SENSOR\"), title: str(vars.title_label, \"DWG A-01  SCALE 1:1\")\n            };\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.1, 4);\n\n            var MONO = \"ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, Consolas, monospace\";\n            var u = Math.min(W, H) / 720;\n            var box = [0.17, 0.6], calloutAt = [0.5, 0.11];\n            var cx = W * 0.47, cy = H * 0.46, bw = box[0] * W, bh = box[1] * H;\n            var x0 = cx - bw / 2, x1 = cx + bw / 2, y0 = cy - bh / 2, y1 = cy + bh / 2;\n            var radius = Math.min(bw, bh) * 0.16;\n            var dotP = { x: x0 + calloutAt[0] * bw, y: y0 + calloutAt[1] * bh };\n            var stroke = 2.4 * u, thin = 1.2 * u, tick = 7 * u;\n            var dimY = y1 + 0.08 * H, dimX = x1 + 0.06 * W;\n            var ring = Math.min(bw, bh) * 0.11;\n            var labelWidth = text.callout.length * 11.8 * u + 26 * u;\n            var sideways = x0 - 0.14 * W - labelWidth > 0.03 * W;\n            var lead = sideways ? { x: x0 - 0.14 * W, y: y0 + 0.06 * H } : { x: Math.max(0.06 * W, dotP.x - 0.1 * W), y: Math.max(0.08 * H, y0 - 0.1 * H) };\n            var elbow = sideways ? \"L \" + (lead.x + 0.06 * W) + \" \" + lead.y + \" H \" + lead.x : \"L \" + lead.x + \" \" + lead.y;\n            var minor = 22 * u;\n            function setBox(svg) { svg.setAttribute(\"viewBox\", \"0 0 \" + W + \" \" + H); }\n\n            // Product before the wipe: a soft shadow, a rounded body and a dark sensor.\n            var prod = document.getElementById(\"bp-product\");\n            setBox(prod);\n            el(\"rect\", { x: x0, y: y0 + 10 * u, width: bw, height: bh, rx: radius, fill: \"#000\", opacity: 0.12, style: \"filter: blur(\" + 14 * u + \"px)\" }, prod);\n            el(\"rect\", { x: x0, y: y0, width: bw, height: bh, rx: radius, fill: productColor }, prod);\n            el(\"circle\", { cx: dotP.x, cy: dotP.y, r: bw * 0.06, fill: \"#111111\" }, prod);\n\n            // The technical drawing, revealed left to right.\n            var sheet = document.getElementById(\"bp-sheet\");\n            setBox(sheet);\n            var defs = el(\"defs\", {}, sheet);\n            var pat = el(\"pattern\", { id: \"bp-grid\", width: minor * 5, height: minor * 5, patternUnits: \"userSpaceOnUse\" }, defs);\n            var gd = \"\";\n            for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) gd += \"M \" + i * minor + \" 0 V \" + minor * 5 + \" M 0 \" + i * minor + \" H \" + minor * 5 + \" \";\n            el(\"path\", { d: gd, stroke: lineColor, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.09, \"stroke-width\": u }, pat);\n            el(\"path\", { d: \"M 0 0 V \" + minor * 5 + \" M 0 0 H \" + minor * 5, stroke: lineColor, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.22, \"stroke-width\": u }, pat);\n            el(\"rect\", { width: W, height: H, fill: blueprintColor }, sheet);\n            el(\"rect\", { width: W, height: H, fill: \"url(#bp-grid)\" }, sheet);\n            var g = el(\"g\", { fill: \"none\", stroke: lineColor, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\" }, sheet);\n            function dashed(node) { node.setAttribute(\"pathLength\", 1); node.setAttribute(\"stroke-dasharray\", 1); return node; }\n            var outlines = [\n              dashed(el(\"rect\", { x: x0, y: y0, width: bw, height: bh, rx: radius, \"stroke-width\": stroke }, g)),\n              dashed(el(\"rect\", { x: x0 + bw * 0.07, y: y0 + bw * 0.07, width: bw * 0.86, height: bh - bw * 0.14, rx: radius * 0.7, \"stroke-width\": thin, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.7 }, g)),\n              dashed(el(\"circle\", { cx: dotP.x, cy: dotP.y, r: bw * 0.06, \"stroke-width\": stroke }, g))\n            ];\n            var center = el(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + cx + \" \" + (y0 - 0.05 * H) + \" V \" + (y1 + 0.05 * H) + \" M \" + (x0 - 0.04 * W) + \" \" + cy + \" H \" + (x1 + 0.04 * W), \"stroke-width\": thin, \"stroke-dasharray\": 14 * u + \" \" + 4 * u + \" \" + 3 * u + \" \" + 4 * u }, g);\n            var ext = el(\"path\", { \"stroke-width\": thin, \"stroke-opacity\": 0.8 }, g);\n            var dimLines = el(\"path\", { \"stroke-width\": thin * 1.3 }, g);\n            var ticks = [[x0, dimY], [x1, dimY], [dimX, y0], [dimX, y1]].map(function (p) {\n              return el(\"line\", { x1: p[0] - tick, y1: p[1] + tick, x2: p[0] + tick, y2: p[1] - tick, \"stroke-width\": stroke, opacity: 0 }, g);\n            });\n            var labels = el(\"g\", { \"font-family\": MONO, \"font-size\": 17 * u, \"letter-spacing\": 1.5 * u, fill: lineColor, opacity: 0 }, sheet);\n            el(\"rect\", { x: cx - 62 * u, y: dimY - 12 * u, width: 124 * u, height: 24 * u, fill: blueprintColor }, labels);\n            el(\"text\", { x: cx, y: dimY + 6 * u, \"text-anchor\": \"middle\" }, labels).textContent = text.width;\n            if (bh > 190 * u) {\n              var vg = el(\"g\", { transform: \"translate(\" + dimX + \" \" + cy + \") rotate(-90)\" }, labels);\n              el(\"rect\", { x: -66 * u, y: -12 * u, width: 132 * u, height: 24 * u, fill: blueprintColor }, vg);\n              el(\"text\", { y: 6 * u, \"text-anchor\": \"middle\" }, vg).textContent = text.height;\n            } else el(\"text\", { x: dimX + 16 * u, y: cy + 6 * u }, labels).textContent = text.height;\n            var tb = el(\"g\", { transform: \"translate(\" + (W - 0.05 * W) + \" \" + (H - 0.06 * H) + \")\" }, labels);\n            el(\"rect\", { x: -290 * u, y: -40 * u, width: 290 * u, height: 40 * u, fill: \"none\", stroke: lineColor, \"stroke-width\": thin }, tb);\n            el(\"text\", { x: -276 * u, y: -14 * u, \"font-size\": 14 * u }, tb).textContent = text.title;\n            // Red callout.\n            var cg = el(\"g\", { stroke: calloutColor, fill: \"none\", \"stroke-width\": stroke, \"stroke-linecap\": \"round\" }, sheet);\n            var leaderParts = [\n              dashed(el(\"circle\", { cx: dotP.x, cy: dotP.y, r: ring }, cg)),\n              dashed(el(\"path\", { d: \"M \" + (dotP.x - ring * 0.72) + \" \" + (dotP.y - ring * 0.72) + \" \" + elbow }, cg))\n            ];\n            var bubbleEl = el(\"circle\", { cx: lead.x, cy: lead.y, r: 0, fill: calloutColor, stroke: \"none\" }, cg);\n            var ct = el(\"g\", { \"font-family\": MONO, opacity: 0 }, sheet);\n            el(\"text\", { x: lead.x, y: lead.y + 6 * u, \"text-anchor\": \"middle\", \"font-size\": 16 * u, \"font-weight\": 700, fill: lineColor }, ct).textContent = \"A\";\n            el(\"text\", { x: sideways ? lead.x - 26 * u : lead.x + 26 * u, y: lead.y + 6 * u, \"text-anchor\": sideways ? \"end\" : \"start\", \"font-size\": 17 * u, \"letter-spacing\": 1.5 * u, fill: lineColor }, ct).textContent = text.callout;\n\n            var scan = document.getElementById(\"bp-scan\");\n            scan.style.width = 4 * u + \"px\";\n            scan.style.backgroundColor = lineColor;\n            scan.style.boxShadow = \"0 0 \" + 24 * u + \"px \" + 6 * u + \"px \" + lineColor;\n            var drawing = document.getElementById(\"bp-drawing\");\n\n            var inOut = E.inOut(E.cubic), popEase = E.out(E.back(2));\n            function ease(t, a, b) { return interp(t, [a, b], [0, 1], { easing: inOut }); }\n            function half(a, b, p) { return [(a + b) / 2 - ((b - a) / 2) * p, (a + b) / 2 + ((b - a) / 2) * p]; }\n            function setDraw(node, p) { node.setAttribute(\"stroke-dashoffset\", 1 - p); node.setAttribute(\"opacity\", p > 0 ? 1 : 0); }\n\n            function draw(frame) {\n              var t = frame * speed;\n              var wipe = interp(t, [6, 24], [-0.04, 1.04], { easing: inOut });\n              var wipeX = wipe * W;\n              var outline = ease(t, 8, 28), extension = ease(t, 22, 28), dims = ease(t, 24, 32);\n              var label = ease(t, 30, 36), leader = ease(t, 32, 40), calloutText = ease(t, 38, 44);\n              var bubble = interp(t, [36, 42], [0, 1], { easing: popEase });\n              drawing.style.clipPath = \"inset(0 \" + (W - wipeX) + \"px 0 0)\";\n              scan.style.left = wipeX - 2 * u + \"px\";\n              scan.style.opacity = wipe > 0 && wipe < 1 ? 0.9 : 0;\n              outlines.forEach(function (o) { setDraw(o, outline); });\n              center.setAttribute(\"stroke-opacity\", 0.55 * outline);\n              ext.setAttribute(\"d\", \"M \" + x0 + \" \" + (y1 + 8 * u) + \" V \" + (y1 + 8 * u + (dimY - y1) * extension) + \" M \" + x1 + \" \" + (y1 + 8 * u) + \" V \" + (y1 + 8 * u + (dimY - y1) * extension) +\n                \" M \" + (x1 + 8 * u) + \" \" + y0 + \" H \" + (x1 + 8 * u + (dimX - x1) * extension) + \" M \" + (x1 + 8 * u) + \" \" + y1 + \" H \" + (x1 + 8 * u + (dimX - x1) * extension));\n              var hh = half(x0, x1, dims), vv = half(y0, y1, dims);\n              dimLines.setAttribute(\"d\", \"M \" + hh[0] + \" \" + dimY + \" H \" + hh[1] + \" M \" + dimX + \" \" + vv[0] + \" V \" + vv[1]);\n              ticks.forEach(function (tk) { tk.setAttribute(\"opacity\", dims > 0.98 ? 1 : 0); });\n              labels.setAttribute(\"opacity\", label);\n              leaderParts.forEach(function (o) { setDraw(o, leader); });\n              bubbleEl.setAttribute(\"r\", 16 * u * bubble);\n              ct.setAttribute(\"opacity\", calloutText);\n            }\n            drive(Math.round(parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.5\") * FPS), draw);\n\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.5\");\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"blueprint\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
